{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>ואושרנא</b> — from the root דלג שור [to leap/bound], and the alef is added like the alef of אזרוע." "<b>בה זמנא, לבנא</b> — the meaning is להבנות [to build]." "<b>ואושרנא</b> — like the meaning of שורא."], :book :ezra, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra parses the Aramaic word by analogy to a Hebrew root and an Aramaic noun form; both comparison terms are left in Hebrew script as he cites them.", 1 "He glosses the Aramaic לבנא by citing the Hebrew infinitive construct להבנות.", 2 "The word שורא may refer to a wall or structure; the comparison term is left untranslated as Ibn Ezra cites it without further specification."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Ezra -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:42:00.487782196Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}